      "heading": "B — Audience, level and prerequisites: hazardous driving conditions",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience, level and prerequisites: hazardous driving conditions\nAudience: first-time North Carolina applicants preparing for the regular Class C knowledge test, in English; the headlight visibility trigger [A02] and the flood water depths [A04] are exact-number recall items.\nLevel: two state laws (headlights at night or short visibility, and headlights with wipers) plus condition-by-condition safe responses; scenario drills fit hydroplaning, fog and flooded roads.\nPrerequisites: the speed and following-distance section and the vehicle equipment section, since tires, wipers and lights recur here.\nSensitivity: flood and hydroplaning guidance is safety-critical and stated as printed.\n",
